# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit the real file — .gitignore already
# blocks it, and a key pushed to a public repo is scraped within hours.
# If one ever does get committed, rotate it in the Sarvam dashboard; deleting
# the commit is not enough, it stays in history.
#
# One key for every service. Defaults: saaras:v4 (STT), sarvam-vision (OCR),
# gemma4 (screen), glm5.3 (extract/propose), sarvam-translate:v1 (translation),
# bulbul:v4-flash (Hindi/English speech), bulbul:v3 (other supported languages).
# V2 chat models require Sarvam beta access; verify your key is enabled.
SARVAM_API_KEY=

# Optional per-task overrides. Omit these to use the defaults above.
# Chat choices: glm5.3, deepseekv4.1-flash, gemma4, sarvam-105b,
# sarvam-105b-conversations. Task settings override SARVAM_CHAT_MODEL.
# SARVAM_SCREEN_MODEL=gemma4
# SARVAM_EXTRACT_MODEL=glm5.3
# SARVAM_PROPOSE_MODEL=glm5.3
# Legacy override for all three chat tasks (also supports keys without V2):
# SARVAM_CHAT_MODEL=sarvam-105b
# SARVAM_STT_MODEL=saaras:v4
# SARVAM_TRANSLATION_MODEL=sarvam-translate:v1
# Speech: auto or bulbul:v4-flash uses v4 only for verified Hindi/English
# personas; other supported languages retain v3. bulbul:v3 forces v3 for all.
# SARVAM_TTS_MODEL=auto
